  "summary": "Package posts host/process data to a hardcoded Telegram bot endpoint at install/runtime",
  "details": "The package ships multiple scripts (setup.js, health.js, bot.js) that combine child_process/fs/os reads with outbound HTTPS to a hardcoded Telegram Bot API endpoint (https://api.telegram.org/bot<redacted>/sendMessage). setup.js runs at configuration/install time and performs POST/https.request calls carrying process.env and process.platform-derived data; health.js issues https.get to api.telegram.org while reading process.env and process.version; bot.js reads directories via fs.readdirSync/fs.existsSync and sends data over https. core/media.js and core/handlers.js additionally combine child_process with outbound POST calls (including hostname and whoami output). The destination is an author-controlled Telegram bot rather than a caller-configurable service, and the data collected includes environment variables and host identity fields that the installer did not opt into sharing.",
